    "title": "Free agency, trades, offer sheets: Do the Hawks have any more surprises? - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Scott Powers Mark Lazerus ,\n1 days ago The annual free-agent frenzy is shaping up to be a spectacular spree of ill-advised spending, as the rising salary cap has given teams a ton of money to play with and very few worthwhile players to spend it on. Even before Alex Tuch and Darryn Raddysh came off the board, this was arguably the worst free-agent class in modern NHL history. But that won’t stop teams from spending big money on the likes of Mason Marchment and Michael Bunting. Read full article",
